        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2d9c683e-abd6-55e9-bc03-a9b6dd77d92d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Languages: Tugurt, Tumzabt, Teggargrent, Berber languages\n- Places: Oued Righ, Touggourt, Algeria, Tamacine\n- Language families and writing systems: Afroasiatic, Libyco-Berber script, Tifinagh\n\nFacts:\n- The Berber languages constitute a branch of the Afroasiatic family.\n- The Berber languages were traditionally written with the ancient Libyco-Berber script, which now exists in the form of Tifinagh.\n- Tugurt is a Zenati Berber variety also known as Oued Righ Berber and Temacine Tamazight.\n- Tugurt is spoken in some oases of the northeastern Oued Righ region around Touggourt in Algeria.\n- Tugurt is also spoken by some residents of Tamacine.\n- Tugurt is closely related to the nearby Tumzabt (Mozabite) and Teggargrent (Ouargli) languages.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
