        "text": "Page: Tugurt language. Sentence: The Tugurt language, also known as Oued Righ Berber and Temacine Tamazight, is a Zenati Berber variety spoken in some of the oases of the northeastern Oued Righ region around Touggourt in Algeria.\nPage: Tugurt language. Sentence: It is closely related to the nearby Tumzabt (Mozabite) and Teggargrent (Ouargli) languages.\nPage: Berber languages. Sentence: The Berber languages constitute a branch of the Afroasiatic family.\nPage: Berber languages. Sentence: They were traditionally written with the ancient Libyco-Berber script, which now exists in the form of Tifinagh.\nPage: Tamacine. Sentence: The Tugurt language is spoken by some residents of Tamacine.",
